     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<div><br></div><div>the man page for geom_map says that it accepts data.frames with column names &quot;long&quot; and &quot;lat&quot; for &quot;x&quot; and &quot;y&quot;</div><div><br></div><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left-width:1px;border-left-color:rgb(204,204,204);border-left-style:solid;padding-left:1ex\"> It must contain columns x or long, y or lat, and region or id.<br></blockquote><div><br></div><div>But that is a dastardly lie :) </div><div><br></div></div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">&gt; Landkreis.DT</font></div></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">            long      lat  order  hole piece   group    id</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">     1: 11.37456 48.68977 261199 FALSE     1 09161.1 09161</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">...</font></div></div><div><div><br></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">&gt; ggplot(values) + geom_map(aes(map_id = id), map = Landkreis.DT) +</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">+ expand_limits(Landkreis.DT)</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" color=\"#cc0000\">Error in exists(name, envir = env, mode = mode) : </font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" color=\"#cc0000\">  argument &quot;env&quot; is missing, with no default</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><br></font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">&gt; setnames(Landkreis.DT,c(&quot;long&quot;,&quot;lat&quot;),c(&quot;x&quot;,&quot;y&quot;))</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\"><br></font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">&gt; ggplot(values) + geom_map(aes(map_id = id), map = Landkreis.DT) +</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" color=\"#000000\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\">+ expand_limits(Landkreis.DT)</font></div></div></blockquote><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 40px;border:none;padding:0px\"><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"background-color:rgb(204,204,204)\" color=\"#274e13\">Works</font></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Is this a bug or is something wrong with my Code?</div><div><br></div><div>ggplot 1.0.0 on R 3.1.2</div><div><br></div><div>Thx</div><div>Stefan</div></div>"
